implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY ONCE. M05 changes the shared settings write path and complete_task, so the gate is the full daemon suite, run fresh: `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test`. It must exit 0. Its command, exit code and output tail are the complete_task verification evidence.

Run it in an isolated Linux-native snapshot (mem gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate):
- git archive HEAD of the WHOLE repo;
- overlay ONLY the five owned paths: state/profileRollout.ts, state/profileRollout.test.ts, state/StateManager.ts, tools/completeTask.ts and __e2e__/rolloutControls.e2e.test.ts under packages/moe-daemon/src;
- npm ci under env -i with a Linux-only PATH and NO_COLOR=1, so no MOE_* is set;
- cmp the owned files against the snapshot before citing the run.
Also run `npx tsc --noEmit`, and a scratch tsconfig that type-checks the two new test files. Compare pass and skip counts with the pre-change HEAD baseline. A newly failing test is a regression to fix, never an assertion to weaken.

Prove the tests bite. On a scratch copy, apply all mutants at once first, then the starred ones alone; restore and cmp the bytes after:
- *drop the activationUnsupported throw (G4 red);
- *revert the completeTask expression (S2 row a red);
- activationGaps returns [] (G1, G3 red);
- skip the refused record (G3 red);
- record before validation or for unrelated updates (R2 red);
- classify observe->legacy as null (R3 red);
- strictRetention ignores attempts (S1, S2 red);
- remove the id cap (S1's MCP read shows '[truncated]');
- emit before the record (R1 red).
Record each mutant and its named failing case in the step note.

